{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-the-heck-is-spa-mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What the heck is SPA mode?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For applications that do not require SSR for either SEO, crawlers, or performance reasons, it may be desirable to ship static HTML to your users containing the \"shell\" of your application (or even prerendered HTML for specific routes) that contain the necessary "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"html"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"head"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":" tags to bootstrap your application only on the client."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-use-start-without-ssr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why use Start without SSR?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No SSR doesn't mean giving up server-side features!"}]},{"type":"text","value":" SPA modes actually pair very nicely with server-side features like server functions and/or server routes or even other external APIs. It "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"simply means that the initial document will not contain the fully rendered HTML of your application until it has been rendered on the client using JavaScript"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"benefits-of-spa-mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Benefits of SPA mode"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Easier to deploy"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - A CDN that can serve static assets is all you need."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cheaper"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to host - CDNs are cheap compared to Lambda functions or long-running processes."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-side Only is simpler"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - No SSR means less to go wrong with hydration, rendering, and routing."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"caveats-of-spa-mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Caveats of SPA mode"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Slower time to full content"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Time to full content is longer since all JS must download and execute before anything below the shell can be rendered."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Less SEO friendly"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Robots, crawlers and link unfurlers "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"may"}]},{"type":"text","value":" have a harder time indexing your application unless they are configured to execute JS and your application can render within a reasonable amount of time."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-does-it-work","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How does it work?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After enabling the SPA mode, running a Start build will have an additional prerendering step afterwards to generate the shell. This is done by:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prerendering"}]},{"type":"text","value":" your application's "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"root route only"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where your application would normally render your matched routes, your router's configured "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"pending fallback component is rendered instead"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The resulting HTML is stored to a static HTML page called "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/_shell.html"},{"type":"text","value":" (configurable)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default rewrites are configured to redirect all 404 requests to the SPA mode shell"}]}]}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other routes may also be prerendered and it is recommended to prerender as much as you can in SPA mode, but this is not required for SPA mode to work."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuring-spa-mode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuring SPA mode"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To configure SPA mode, there are a few options you can add to your Start plugin's options:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"bundler"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"vite","data-tab-index":"0","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      spa: {\n        enabled: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"vite.config.ts\"","title":"vite.config.ts","file":"vite.config.ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"rsbuild","data-tab-index":"1","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      spa: {\n        enabled: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"","title"